SELECT import_new_structured_page_v1('3cbdc749-e9c9-44f3-8330-ecc1e3b38cc8'::uuid, '59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7'::uuid, 'a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, '{"pageId": "e0410000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "pageNumber": 41, "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "41", "printedPageNumber": 41, "pdfPageNumber": 424, "sequenceIndex": 31, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en", "ar"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": true, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true}, "structuralNodes": [], "blocks": [{"id": "f0410000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Part I (b)—Warning on Discard of Salaat", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}, {"id": "f0410100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "for neglecting Maghrib and till dawn for neglecting Ishaa. The serpent will keep on thrashing him thus till the Last Day. Each blow pushes him to a depth of seventy arm''s length. The punishments will last till the Day of Judgement.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}, {"id": "f0410200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Those after resurrection are: His reckoning will be a hard one; Allah will be angry with him; and he will be thrown into the Fire. According to one report, he will have following three lines inscribed on his forehead:", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}, {"id": "f0410300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "''O you who neglected Allah''s duty''\n''O you who has deserved Allah''s wrath.''\n''Now despair of Allah''s mercy, as you neglected your duty to Allah.''", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}, {"id": "f0410400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Eminent theologians like Ibn Hajr, Abu Laith Samarqandi (Rahmatullah alaihim), and others, have mentioned this hadith in their books. Although I have not been able to trace the text in original books on hadith, yet other hadiths, some of which have already been mentioned and some are to follow, corroborate its meaning. Neglect of salaat, as has been stated above, leads one to kufr; hence no punishment is too severe for this offence. But it should be borne in mind that even after the declaration of a person as being guilty, Allah is free to pardon him as and when He pleases. He says in His Holy Book:", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}, {"id": "f0410500-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ أَنْ يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَنْ يَشَاءُ", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}, {"id": "f0410600-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 6, "blockType": "translation", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "\"Lo! Allah pardoneth not that partners should be ascribed unto Him. Allah pardoneth all (save that) whom He will. (IV: 116)\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}, {"id": "f0410700-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 7, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "If then it pleases Allah to pardon anybody neglecting salaat, it will be most fortunate; but who can be sure of this fortune?", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}, {"id": "f0410800-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 8, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "It is also stated in hadith that there will be three courts to be held by Allah on the Day of Judgement. The first will judge between kufr and islaam and there will be no pardon. The second will be to judge the duties and conduct of one towards another. All aggrieved shall be compensated there; compensation will either be realised from the aggressor or paid by Allah Himself, if He pleases to pardon anybody. The third will deal with duties towards Allah. Here the doors of Allah''s mercy will be thrown wide-open and He shall pardon anybody He wills. In the light of all that has", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 41"}]}'::jsonb);
SELECT import_new_structured_page_v1('3cbdc749-e9c9-44f3-8330-ecc1e3b38cc8'::uuid, '59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7'::uuid, 'a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, '{"pageId": "e0420000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "pageNumber": 42, "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "42", "printedPageNumber": 42, "pdfPageNumber": 425, "sequenceIndex": 32, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": false, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true}, "structuralNodes": [], "blocks": [{"id": "f0420000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Virtues of Salaat", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "been said above, it must be clearly understood that we deserve the punishments that have been laid down for our commission of sins, but the All-embracing mercy of Allah overrides everything and knows no bounds.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "It was a habit with the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) to enquire from the companions, just after Fajr, if anybody had seen any dream. He would then interpret the dream as related to him. One day, after enquiring from others as usual, the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) himself narrated a long dream in which two men came and took him with them. Besides others he reported certain events which he happened to see in his dream. He said: \"I noticed the head of a person being crushed with a heavy stone. It was struck with such force that, after crushing the head, the stone rolled down over a long distance. The head would assume its normal shape by the time the stone was brought back for repeating the process. This continued incessantly. On inquiring from one of my companions, I was told that the person first learnt the Qur''an, but failed to practise upon it and also used to go to sleep without offering the fardh salaat.\" There is another similar narration, in which the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is reported to have seen (in his dream) a group of people being treated likewise. Jibra-eel (Alayhis salaam) informed him on his query that those were the persons who used to neglect their salaat.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Mujahid (Rahmatullah alaih) says, \"Allah blesses the people who guard their salaat, just as He blessed Hadhrat Ibrahim (Alayhis salaam) and his descendants.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Anas (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"If a person dies with sincere Imaan, observing the commandments of Allah, performing salaat, and paying Zakaat, when he dies Allah is pleased with him.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420500-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Anas (Radhiyallaho anho) also narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"Allah says, ''I hold back retribution, deserved by a locality, when I see therein some people who frequently visit the musjid, love one another for My sake, and pray for forgiveness in the hours of darkness.''\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}, {"id": "f0420600-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 6, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Abu Darda (Radhiyallaho anho) wrote to Hadhrat Salmaan: \"Spend most of your time in the musjid. I have heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, ''The musjid is the abode of the pious. Allah has taken upon Himself to bless the person who spends most of", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 42"}]}'::jsonb);
SELECT import_new_structured_page_v1('3cbdc749-e9c9-44f3-8330-ecc1e3b38cc8'::uuid, '59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7'::uuid, 'a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, '{"pageId": "e0430000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "pageNumber": 43, "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "43", "printedPageNumber": 43, "pdfPageNumber": 426, "sequenceIndex": 33, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en", "ar"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": true, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true}, "structuralNodes": [], "blocks": [{"id": "f0430000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Part I (b)—Warning on Discard of Salaat", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}, {"id": "f0430100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "his time in the mosque. Allah shall keep him in comfort and shall make him cross the Siraat with great ease. Surely Allah is pleased with such a person.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}, {"id": "f0430200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Abdullah bin Mas''ood (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying: \"The masaajid are the Houses of Allah, and people coming therein are His visitors. When everybody treats his visitors kindly, why should Allah not be kind to His guests?\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}, {"id": "f0430300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Abu Sa''eed Khudri (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying: \"Allah loves the person who is attached to the musjid.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}, {"id": "f0430400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Abu Hurairah (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"When a dead person is laid in the grave, even before the people present at his burial clear off, Munkar and Nakeer visit him. Then, if the person is a Mo''min, his good practices encircle him; salaat comes close to his head, Zakaat to his right, Fast to his left, and the remaining good deeds towards his feet, so that none can approach him. Even the angels do the necessary questioning while standing at a distance.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}, {"id": "f0430500-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "One of the companions reports that, when the inmates of the Prophet''s house were hard-pressed in any way, he would enjoin salaat on them and recite the following verse:", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}, {"id": "f0430600-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 6, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "وَأْمُرْ أَهْلَكَ بِالصَّلَاةِ وَاصْطَبِرْ عَلَيْهَا لَا نَسْأَلُكَ رِزْقًا نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُكَ وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلتَّقْوَى", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}, {"id": "f0430700-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 7, "blockType": "translation", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "\"And enjoin salaat upon thy people and be constant therein. We ask not of thee a provision, We provide for thee. And the Hereafter is for the righteousness.\" (XX: 132).", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}, {"id": "f0430800-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 8, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Asma (Radhiyallaho anha) narrates that she heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"All the people will be gathered together on the Day of Judgement and they will all hear the voice of the announcing angel. He will say, ''where are those who glorified Allah in ease and adversity?'' A group will rise up and enter Paradise without reckoning. It will then be announced, ''where are those who forsook their beds and spent their nights in worship?'' Another group will rise up and enter Paradise without reckoning. The angel will again announce, ''where", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 43"}]}'::jsonb);
SELECT import_new_structured_page_v1('3cbdc749-e9c9-44f3-8330-ecc1e3b38cc8'::uuid, '59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7'::uuid, 'a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, '{"pageId": "e0440000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "pageNumber": 44, "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "44", "printedPageNumber": 44, "pdfPageNumber": 427, "sequenceIndex": 34, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": false, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true}, "structuralNodes": [], "blocks": [{"id": "f0440000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Virtues of Salaat", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 44"}, {"id": "f0440100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "are those whom trade and business did not distract from remembrance of Allah?'' Yet another group will rise up and enter Paradise.\" In another hadith, the same account is given, with the addition that in the beginning the angel will say, \"All those gathered here will see today who are the honoured people\", and with the modification that the angel at the time of third announcement will say, ''Where are those whom their engagement in trade and business did not distract from salaat and remembrance of Allah?''", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 44"}, {"id": "f0440200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Sheik Nasr Samarqandi (Rahmatullah alaih), after quoting this Hadith writes, \"When all the three groups will have entered Paradise without reckoning, a monster with a long neck, shining eyes and most eloquent tongue will rise up from Hell and say, ''I have been deputed on all who are proud and ill-tempered.'' It will then pick up all such persons from the crowd, as a fowl picks up grain and then it will fling them into the Hell. It will rise up again saying, ''This time I have been deputed on all who maligned Allah and His Apostle (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam).'' It will then pick up all such persons and throw them into the Hell; it will appear for the third time and will, in a similar manner, take away all those who made images and pictures. The reckoning will then commence after these three groups have been eliminated.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 44"}, {"id": "f0440300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "It is said that during the early times people could see Satan. A person approached him saying how could he be like him. Satan told him that he had never received such a request before and asked him what had prompted him to ask for it. The person told him that he wished it from his heart. Satan told him to neglect his salaat and to swear very frequently, not caring whether he was doing it truthfully. The person told Satan that he would swear by Allah never to give up salaat and swear falsely. Satan told him that never before had he been tricked by a human being to seek his advice. He was determined never to do so in future.", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 44"}, {"id": "f0440400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Ubayy (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"Give glad tidings to the Muslims that they shall be honoured and exalted, and their religion shall prevail, but there is no portion in the Hereafter for those who exploit Islam for worldly gains.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 44"}, {"id": "f0440500-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is reported to have said, \"I saw Allah in His best form. He said to me, ''O Muhammad! what are the Highest Chiefs (Angels) arguing about?'' I said, ''I have no knowledge about that.'' Allah", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 44"}]}'::jsonb);
SELECT import_new_structured_page_v1('3cbdc749-e9c9-44f3-8330-ecc1e3b38cc8'::uuid, '59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7'::uuid, 'a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001'::uuid, 'a4000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'::uuid, '{"pageId": "e0450000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "pageNumber": 45, "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "45", "printedPageNumber": 45, "pdfPageNumber": 428, "sequenceIndex": 35, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en", "ar"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": true, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true}, "structuralNodes": [], "blocks": [{"id": "f0450000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Part I (b)—Warning on Discard of Salaat", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 45"}, {"id": "f0450100-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "placed His gracious hand on my bosom. I felt its solacing coolness right through my heart, and the entire universe was revealed to me. I said, ''They are arguing about the things which exalt, the things which atone for the sins, the rewards for the paces taken while going for salaat (with Jamaat), the virtues of performing wudhu properly when it was very cold, and the blessings that a person deserves when after performing one salaat he keeps on sitting in musjid till the next salaat.'' A person particular of these shall live a blessed life and shall die an enviable death.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 45"}, {"id": "f0450200-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is reported (in many ahaadith) to have said, \"Allah says, ''O, Son of Aadam! Say four rakaats of salaat in the early part of the day. I shall help thee in accomplishing all thy jobs during the rest of the day.''\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 45"}, {"id": "f0450300-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "It is said in a hadith: \"Salaat is the cause of Allah''s pleasure, is loved by the Angels, is a tradition of the Prophets, gives enlightenment about Allah, causes the prayers to be granted, blesses the daily bread, is the root of Imaan, refreshes the body, is a weapon against the enemy, shall intercede for its adherent, is a light in the darkness and a companion in the loneliness of the grave, is a reply to the questioning of Angels, is a shade against the Sun on the Day of Judgement, is a protection against the fire of Hell, is a weight for the scales of good deeds, is a means of swift crossing over the Siraat and is a key to Paradise.\"", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 45"}, {"id": "f0450400-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Uthman (Radhiyallaho anho) is reported to have said, \"Allah bestows nine favours on a person who guards his salaat and is particular in performing it at its appointed hours: viz: He is loved by Allah, he enjoys good health, is constantly under the protection of angels, his home is blessed, the light of righteousness shines on his face, his heart is made soft, he shall cross the Siraat with the speed of lightning, he is saved from Hell, and his neighbours in Paradise are those about whom Allah has said,", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 45"}, {"id": "f0450500-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 5, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "أَلَا إِنَّ أَوْلِيَاءَ اللَّهِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 45"}, {"id": "f0450600-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 6, "blockType": "translation", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "''There shall be no fear come upon them, neither shall they grieve (II: 36).''", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 45"}, {"id": "f0450700-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": null, "sequenceIndex": 7, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) says, \"Salaat is the Pillar of Islam and it has ten virtues, viz: It is a charm of the face, a light of the heart, health and refreshment for the body, a company in the grave, a means for the descent", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "provenanceNotes": "Locked human-reviewed handoff: printed page 45"}]}'::jsonb);